10 General Ledger Enquiry

Purpose

The General Ledger Enquiry module is designed to allow users to search and view GL balances and transaction details based on the selected enquiry criteria. Users can filter the required information and export the results as an Excel file.

When the user clicks on General Ledger Enquiry from the side bar, the General Ledger Enquiry screen is displayed with four enquiry options:

    • GLCC Balance Enquiry: To view balance details for a selected GLCC and date range.
    • GLCC Transaction Enquiry: To view transaction details for a selected GLCC, transaction type and date range.
    • GL Account Enquiry: To view transaction details based on Circle, Branch, CGL, Currency and Transaction Type.
    • GL Balance Enquiry: To view balance details based on the selected Enquiry Type, Circle, Branch, CGL, Currency and Balance Date.


10.1 GLCC Balance Enquiry

The GLCC Balance Enquiry allows users to search and view balance details based on GLCC or individual Branch, Currency and CGL selections.

[Insert Screenshot – GLCC Balance Enquiry]


Search GLCC Balance

    • User can directly enter the GLCC or provide the Branch, Currency and CGL individually.
    • Branch can be selected using the search option by providing the Branch Code or Branch Name.
    • Select the required Currency.
    • Select the required CGL.
    • Select the required Date Range.
    • If Custom Range is selected, select or enter the From Date and To Date.
    • Click Search to view the balance details.

Note: Ensure all mandatory fields are completed before performing the search.

The application displays the balance details based on the selected criteria.

If no records are available, the application displays the message:

“No balance records available for the selected criteria”.


Reset

Click Reset to clear the selected values and return the screen to its default state.


Export

Click Export to download the displayed balance details as an Excel file.

