10.2 GLCC Transaction Enquiry

The GLCC Transaction Enquiry allows users to search and view transaction details based on GLCC or individual Branch, Currency, CGL and Transaction Type selections.

[Insert Screenshot – GLCC Transaction Enquiry]


Search GLCC Transactions

    • User can directly enter the GLCC or provide the Branch, Currency and CGL individually.
    • Branch can be selected using the search option by providing the Branch Code or Branch Name.
    • Select the required Currency.
    • Select the required CGL.
    • Select the required Transaction Type. The default selection is All.
    • Select the required Date Range.
    • If Custom Range is selected, select or enter the From Date and To Date.
    • User can optionally enter From Amount and To Amount to search for transactions within a specific amount range.
    • Click Search to view the transaction details.

Note: Ensure all mandatory fields are completed before performing the search.

The application displays the transaction details based on the selected criteria.

If no records are available, the application displays the message:

“No transactions available for the selected criteria”.


Reset

Click Reset to clear the selected values and return the screen to its default state.


Export

Click Export to download the displayed transaction details as an Excel file.

[Insert Screenshot – GLCC Transaction Enquiry Results]


10.3 GL Account Enquiry

The GL Account Enquiry allows users to search and view transaction details based on Circle, Branch, CGL, Currency and Transaction Type.

[Insert Screenshot – GL Account Enquiry]


Search GL Account Transactions

    • Select the required Circle. The default selection is All Circles.
    • Select the required Branch. The default selection is All Branches.
    • Select the required CGL.
    • Select the required Currency. The default selection is All Currencies.
    • Select the required Transaction Type. The default selection is All Transaction Types.
    • Select the required Date Range.
    • If Custom Range is selected, select or enter the From Date and To Date.
    • Click Search to view the transaction details.

Note: Ensure all mandatory fields are completed before performing the search.

The application displays the transaction details based on the selected criteria.

If no records are available, the application displays the message:

“No transactions available for the selected criteria”.


Reset

Click Reset to clear the selected values and return the fields to their default selections.

The Reset option sets the Transaction Type, Circle and Currency to their default options.


Table Filtering

Users can apply filters to the transaction data displayed in the table.


Export

Click Export to download the displayed transaction details as an Excel file.

[Insert Screenshot – GL Account Enquiry Results]


10.4 GL Balance Enquiry

The GL Balance Enquiry allows users to search and view balance details based on the selected Enquiry Type, Circle, Branch, CGL, Currency and Balance Date.

[Insert Screenshot – GL Balance Enquiry]


Search GL Balance

    • Select the required Enquiry Type. The default Enquiry Type is Collation.
    • Select the required Circle. The default selection is All Circles.
    • For Collation, select the required Branch. The default selection is All Branches.
    • Select the required CGL. The default selection is All CGLs.
    • Select the required Currency. The default selection is All Currencies.
    • Select the required Balance Date.
    • Click Search to view the balance details.


Consolidation

When the Enquiry Type is selected as Consolidation, the user can select the required Circle.

The Branch selection will not be available for Consolidation.

[Insert Screenshot – GL Balance Enquiry Consolidation]


The application displays the balance details based on the selected criteria.

If no records are available, the application displays the message:

“No balances available for the selected criteria”.


Reset

Click Reset to clear the selected values and return the screen to its default state.


Table Filtering

Users can apply filters to the balance data displayed in the table.


Export

Click Export to download the displayed balance details as an Excel file.

